implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (red). First read the LANDED C08 (task-f12b03e8) recipe framework and adapt every name below to its interface: its definition record, its kind registry, its eligibility/fallback reason shape and any post-patch hook. Then create docsLiteralReplace.test.ts using real temp Git repos, following the fixture style of context/repositorySource.test.ts; no mocks for Git. Assert exact reason codes and exact objects, never truthiness.
(DoD1) Eligible only when sha256 of the COMMITTED bytes at the basis commit equals originalSha256 AND oldText occurs exactly once. Refusals:
- docs-replace-hash-mismatch;
- docs-replace-old-text-missing;
- docs-replace-old-text-ambiguous, including an overlapping repeat ('aa' in 'aaa');
- docs-replace-source-unavailable, for a missing path, a symlink, a 100755 file, binary or non-UTF-8 bytes, a file over the byte cap, and an unresolvable commit.
(DoD2) The definition is refused when allowedPaths or requiredChecks is missing or empty. An input path outside allowedPaths, under .moe/, or not *.md gives docs-replace-path-not-allowed. The instantiated plan is exactly one step with affectedFiles [path]. Its executionContract.requiredChecks deep-equals the definition's checks, checkRefs equals their commands, and approvedScope names only the path.
(DoD3) Post-patch:
- exactly [path] changed with the expected post sha256 passes;
- another path changed gives docs-replace-extra-edits, listing the paths;
- an extra change inside the same file gives docs-replace-postpatch-mismatch;
- no change gives docs-replace-patch-missing;
- an inputs digest that differs from the instantiation record gives docs-replace-inputs-changed;
- a definition kind or version that differs from the recipe gives docs-replace-recipe-mismatch;
- a Git failure gives an unavailable reason, and nothing throws.

amendments.description:
TESTS FIRST (red). Build on the LANDED C08 module packages/moe-daemon/src/context/recipes/recipe.ts. The names follow C08's plan and msg-c7ac9a51; adapt them if the landed code differs:
- RecipeKind, recipeKinds, instantiateRecipe;
- RECIPE_DEFINITIONS_PATH ('.moe/recipes.json');
- recipeInputsDigest, recipeDefinitionDigest, readRecipeInstance;
- Task.recipeInstance.

Create docsLiteralReplace.test.ts.

Fixture: copy C08's recipe.test.ts fixture:
- ToolTestHarness;
- a real temp Git repo, with GIT_* masked and fixed identities;
- settings patched in memory, with approvalMode TURBO.
Commit .moe/recipes.json = {version:1, recipes:[DEF]} together with docs/a.md, where DEF = {id:'docs-fix', kind:'docs-literal-replace', version:1, requiredChecks:[{id:'docs', command:'npm run lint'}], params:{allowedPaths:['docs']}}. The recipes file exists only in temp repos, never in the real project. Import docsLiteralReplace.ts so it self-registers.
INPUTS = {path:'docs/a.md', originalSha256:<sha256 of the committed bytes>, oldText, newText}.
Assert exact reasons and exact objects, never truthiness. Keep the cases table-driven (it.each).

(DoD1) instantiateRecipe(h.state, {taskId, recipeId:'docs-fix', inputs:INPUTS}) instantiates only when both hold:
- the sha256 of the committed bytes at the pinned commit equals originalSha256;
- oldText occurs exactly once.
Under TURBO that gives {instantiated:true, status:'WORKING', planRevision}.
Each refusal is the fallback {instantiated:false, fallback:'ordinary-planning', reason}, with the kind's reason verbatim and the row untouched:
- docs-replace-hash-mismatch. Include a worktree-only edit of docs/a.md, which must not count: committed bytes only.
- docs-replace-old-text-missing.
- docs-replace-old-text-ambiguous, including the overlapping repeat 'aa' in 'aaa'.
- docs-replace-source-unavailable, for a missing path, a symlink, a 100755 file, binary or non-UTF-8 bytes, and a file over the provider's 64 KiB cap.

(DoD2) Definition and input refusals:
- docs-replace-definition-invalid: params missing; allowedPaths missing, empty or not normalized; or extra keys in params.
- docs-replace-inputs-invalid: missing, extra or non-string input keys; an originalSha256 that is not 64 lowercase hex; an oldText that is empty or over 2000 chars; a newText over 2000 chars; a NUL; or newText === oldText.
- docs-replace-path-not-allowed: a path outside allowedPaths, under .moe/, or not *.md.
On success:
- The stored plan is exactly one step, with affectedFiles ['docs/a.md'].
- The step text contains 'error handling' and 'test', the project's required rail patterns.
- executionContract.checkRefs equals ['npm run lint'], and approvedScope is exactly ['docs/a.md'].
- requiredChecks deep-equals the definition's checks plus C08's appended '.moe/recipes.json' config. The framework owns requiredChecks; the kind never returns them.
- readRecipeInstance(task) returns the record, with kind 'docs-literal-replace'.

(DoD3) docsLiteralReplace.assessPostpatch(root, {taskId, instance, definition, postCommit}), over real commits built on instance.commit:
- {ok:true} when exactly docs/a.md changed to the expected bytes, and also when the postCommit additionally changes the task's own .moe/tasks/<taskId>.json;
- docs-replace-extra-edits for any other changed path, including .moe/recipes.json;
- docs-replace-postpatch-mismatch for an extra change inside docs/a.md;
- docs-replace-patch-missing when nothing changed;
- docs-replace-inputs-changed for an instance whose inputs no longer match its inputsDigest;
- docs-replace-recipe-mismatch for a definition whose digest, id, kind or version differs from the instance;
- docs-replace-postpatch-unavailable for an unresolvable postCommit;
- nothing throws.

Run npx vitest run src/context/recipes/docsLiteralReplace.test.ts. Every case must fail for the right reason: the missing module.

implementationPlan.description:
Verify once. Iterate with `npx vitest run src/context/recipes/docsLiteralReplace.test.ts`. Then run the gate fresh in an isolated Linux snapshot of HEAD with native deps, MOE_* unset and a Linux-only PATH (see mem:gotcha-daemon-linux-snapshot-gate), plus `npx tsc --noEmit`. The gate is `cd packages/moe-daemon && npm test`, and it must exit 0. Supply its command, exit code and output tail to complete_task. Also prove mutations are killed on scratch copies, then restore and cmp the bytes:
- drop the uniqueness check;
- compare the hash of the worktree instead of committed bytes;
- ignore extra changed paths;
- skip the inputs-digest compare.

One adversarial self-review of this task's diff only. Check:
- CRLF and BOM bytes, and a NUL in oldText;
- oldText overlapping itself, or newText containing oldText;
- path case collisions and a path with traversal or control characters;
- a symlink or gitlink at the path;
- the doc changing between assessSource and postpatch;
- two instantiations of the same task running concurrently;
- a candidate that edits the recipe definition itself;
- Git timeouts.
Confirm that no .moe edits and no Git writes happen, and that legacy (non-recipe) tasks are untouched.
